        "Agencies using outdated technologies like WordPress with heavy page builders create sites that are slow, hard to maintain, and vulnerable to security exploits. In 2026, modern agencies build with React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS — frameworks that deliver superior performance, maintainability, and developer experience. Ask about the tech stack before signing anything. Your website's technology foundation determines its performance ceiling for years to come.",
        "## Demand Transparent Pricing",
        "Beware of agencies that won't give you a clear price range until the first meeting. Professional agencies publish their pricing tiers openly because they're confident in the value they deliver. Look for clear deliverables, timelines, and what's included in each package. Hidden fees for \"SSL certificates,\" \"mobile optimization,\" or \"basic SEO\" are red flags — these should be standard in every modern website.",
        "## Quality Assurance Is Non-Negotiable",
        "Ask directly: \"How do you test before launch?\" If the answer is vague — \"we check it on a couple of browsers\" — walk away. Professional agencies employ structured QA processes, ideally with ISTQB-certified engineers who test across browsers, devices, and operating systems. They perform accessibility audits, check form submissions, validate schema markup, and ensure zero broken links. A flawless launch isn't luck — it's process.",
        "## Communication and Process Transparency",
        "How an agency communicates during the sales process is a preview of how they'll communicate during the project. Do they respond promptly? Do they ask smart questions about your business goals? Do they share their development process? The best agencies offer weekly progress updates, shared project boards, and direct access to your project lead — not a generic support email that takes 72 hours to respond.",
        "## Ongoing Support and Maintenance",
        "A website launch is a beginning, not an end. Ask about post-launch support: Do they offer maintenance packages? How quickly do they respond to urgent issues? Do they provide security updates, performance monitoring, and content updates? An agency that disappears after launch leaves you vulnerable to bugs, security breaches, and an increasingly outdated website.",
        "## Multilingual and International Capabilities",
        "If your business serves Greek and international clients, your agency must understand multilingual web development. This goes beyond Google Translate: proper hreflang tags, localized meta descriptions, culturally appropriate design adaptations, and URL structures that search engines can parse correctly. An agency with proven bilingual experience will save you months of rework.",
        "## Red Flags to Watch For",
        "Avoid agencies that promise unrealistic timelines (\"your full website in 2 days\"), use only template-based solutions claiming them as custom, can't show live examples of their work, don't discuss SEO or performance, or pressure you into long-term contracts before proving their value. Trust your instincts — if something feels off during the sales process, the project experience will be worse.",
